Package: screensense
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: gnome-shell
Description: move focus to the monitor you are looking at
 ScreenSense uses your webcam to see which monitor you are facing, and moves
 keyboard focus, the mouse pointer, or both there, so you do not have to click
 to change screens. It waits while you are typing, and can follow your eyes as
 well as your head.
 .
 Video is processed on this computer only. Nothing is recorded or sent
 anywhere, and the camera is off until you calibrate, while paused and while
 the screen is locked.
 .
 This package contains the background service, which runs as a systemd user
 service, and the GNOME Shell extension that changes focus. GNOME 45 to 50 is
 supported.
